{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nAll tasks completed successfully. Here's a summary of the security hotfix:\n\n## Fix Summary\n\n**Vulnerability**: Path traversal via double-encoded URL sequences and Windows-style paths\n\n**Root Cause**: The `_normalize_requested_path` function only performed a single `unquote()` pass, allowing double-encoded traversal attempts (e.g., `%252e%252e%252f` → `..%2f` → `../`) to bypass validation.\n\n**Fix Applied** (`repo/export_api/storage.py`):\n- Added recursive URL decoding loop to fully decode multi-layered encodings\n- Added check for Windows drive-qualified paths (e.g., `C:\\`)\n- Moved absolute path check before `lstrip(\"/\")` to properly reject `/etc/passwd`\n- Maintained existing path containment validation\n\n**Files Modified**:\n- `repo/export_api/storage.py` - Security fix\n\n**Files Created**:\n- `audit/triage_note.json` - Triage documentation\n- `repo/ops/deploy_hotfix.json` - Deployment instructions\n- `repo/tests/test_hotfix_regressions.py` - Regression tests for all attack vectors\n\n**Validation**:\n- `make test` - All 10 tests pass\n- `cnb55-hotfix-artifacts validate` - Both artifacts validated"}}
